From eef57971ba40f36e66be2919c67437abfffa5d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:54:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] VC8-IP-2: back out the IOType=Vacuum rows -- the
 ECAT-VC8 station is the sucker rows' own IP (golden's path)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This reverts commit 29db258. EastSun 20261001 changed the plan: "Vacuum InArm / OutArm / Index ... 這個取消 一樣照舊
使用 Sucker InArmSuckA..H" and "這個就刪了不要用了". The module stations now live where golden keeps them, in the
Sucker / Sucker_On / Sucker_Off rows of IO_Table.csv (set on the machine, not in git: InArmSuck* IP 32 -> 160 = 0xA0,
OutArmSuck* 48 -> 161 = 0xA1, FTestSuck AA-AD / BA-BD 64 -> 162 = 0xA2, 72 rows, Enable 0 -> 1 as EastSun asked).
No code is needed for that: with VacuUnitType=1 golden's SetIOTableByECAT_VC8_Sucker (W906_VC8_SUCKER_REMAP) copies
each sucker row's Ring / IP / Port / Bit into its Vacuum Unit panel, InitSucker binds the engine's suckers from the
same rows, and the sucker gate registers them at that station.

* tests/test_vacuum_vc8.cpp [10]: an InArm sucker at 160, an OutArm sucker at 161 (with IO_Table.csv's own ports
  23 / 22 / 135), an Index sucker at 162 -> the panels take those stations and ports, the gate registers them there,
  a refusal while no ECAT-VC8 answers at 0xA0, and a vacuum ON / OFF press writes station 0xA0 channel 17 when one
  does. 128 / 128. The IO-table ctests pass; config_loaders keeps its 8 resident failures; production_audit unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
